t body part and we did it first. I don't know when women started finding ideal the ass of a man, but if you watch movies as a reflection of society I would say around the late seventies/early eighties. A mans ass has no function to a female, but it happens to be the standard to which we adjudge women, so now all of the sudden we will be held to the same standard. I can't find another reason to rationalize women's affinity to a man's ass, probably arising out of the liberation era.<P>But ultimately I agree with women in their plight to break the age-old male stereotype roles. As a somewhat distant example, when I was in the A.F., I didn't like some prick telling me I had to wear my hair short for no other practical purpose than to establish dominance over me. As well they disallowed us to frequent a head shop. When I got out, I wore my hair military short for several years to follow and have never visited a head shop, so it wasn't me wanting to engage in certain conduct/appearance, it was me not wanting to be ordered to conform to someone else’s standard of ideal, or in this case moral.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Guys love a women’s ass for obvious reasons; its functionality. "<P>How is a wom<B>a</B>n's ass "functional"?<P>"A mans ass has no function to a female, but it happens to be the standard to which we adjudge women, so now all of the sudden we will be held to the same standard. "<P>If a woman<B>'</B>s ass can be "functional", why can't a man<B>'</B>s?<P>Sorry about the quoting, I couldn't resist.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
