Z||000035||AusFiero||08-13-2001||09:47 AM||||Heres a good law I heard about and cracked up over. In England a guy got arrested for trying to commit suicide. The maximum penalty (old law never changed) for this act his death by hanging. Kinda defeats the purpose of saving the person in the first place doesn't it?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000036||Ken Wittlief||08-13-2001||10:10 AM||||Ok I know it sounds crazy to have a law against committing suicide - but there is logic behind it.<P>1. Someone takes out a large insurance policy, and then commits suicide, hoping it will look like an accident and his family benefits. This is fraud and its illegal. There has to be something to tie the act to the fraud - therefore, committing suicide is the illegal act that voids the life insurance.<P>2. someone decides to kill themself in a violent self destructive manner, throwing themself off a building, driving their car into an oncoming truck - other people can be killed or injured in the process. People need to know if they attempt suicide or commit suicide and someone else is injured in the process, then they are accountable, or their estate is held accountable.<P>3. someone decides to commit suicide and asks a friend for help in doing it. Since suicide is a crime, assisted a suicide is also a crime.<P>   Its kinda like those cases where a politician dies just before an election, and is still elected. It sounds stupid, like people want a dead person to serve in public office. But in reality it takes a long time and a lot of paperwork to put someones name on a ballot. If the candiadate dies just before the election and it were not possible to vote for the dead person, then their opponenet would win by default. In most cases the political party of the deceased candiate is allowed to assign the persons replacement - the same as if they had died in office, or a second election is held later.<P>   so even though some of these things sounds stupid at face value - there really are sound reasons behind them.||||reg||10
